@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] admission-evidence-boundary
Admission assertions MUST use a committed result or an independent PostgreSQL
snapshot as their antecedent. A submitted request, lost reply, missing oracle,
or stale report MUST NOT establish success, refusal, or absence of an effect.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity;verification] admission-physical-boundary
Capacity assertions MUST identify the real measured host and pool report used,
account for all startup, temporary-copy, and resize holds, and disclose when
later mutable reports cannot reconstruct the exact admission-time budget.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] admission-closed-operator
Mutation clients MUST invoke only reviewed fixed synthetic fixture actions.
Neither an Antithesis draw nor an external request may select arbitrary actor,
source, command, SQL mutation, or runtime code.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity;verification] admission-stub-substrate-boundary
Commands selected with the stub storage substrate MUST NOT emit assertions
whose messages claim measured ZFS, physical headroom, KVM or isolation, and
MUST NOT read a stub-derived file as an independent physical witness. Their
assertions may claim only Marshall admission effects observed in PostgreSQL.
